{"id": "EUVD-2026-71281", "enisaUuid": "a515f1eb-ebfc-36ab-b231-f33a44cc9284", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncrypto: mxs-dcp - fix source scatterlist length access\n\nmxs_dcp_aes_block_crypt() uses sg_dma_len() without mapping the source\nscatterlist with dma_map_sg() first. Therefore, sg_dma_len() is invalid\nand could return zero or a stale DMA length, causing encryption and\ndecryption to process the wrong number of bytes when\nCONFIG_NEED_SG_DMA_LENGTH=y.\n\nUse the original scatterlist length instead.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:54:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd0f211b27a6ec2ebd8c315683401b43adcc5511", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04201dcc88b26eac52f736e39727fc5c420b7257", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e72a795df521cb65b7c4705cc11078cdacfaa2f4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1537bd55b4f842565068c54b47cd2ae1777d5f8f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/da14fae5203b72ca71ccfa9af8de9249e40d533a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/182f16a20d329a1c818d51dad57d9bf43d356c7c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e9edb108a63bbbef952dfcbc597e34ed9c1fb74", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6ef9a4afb52cb102ab038cd42352c142d8505d09", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c5bcb084a9871e5b62afb5f48b60adfa13b5d9f8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fv42-pvcm-2c76", "CVE-2026-80831"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05077540-bb5c-3fb8-a35b-fabca8eb17a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "15b59e7c3733f90ff1f7dd66ad77ae1c90bcdff5 <e72a795df521cb65b7c4705cc11078cdacfaa2f4"}, {"id": "183ef203-1301-3e37-9918-e0ca1016effd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "15b59e7c3733f90ff1f7dd66ad77ae1c90bcdff5 <0e9edb108a63bbbef952dfcbc597e34ed9c1fb74"}, {"id": "39cebe72-7d0e-38f1-a271-f91cd94414ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux